-- title:
--   Degeneracy legs at ℓ≠ p preserve the Gauss centre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), namely the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ (the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with the compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose $q$-expansion is the image in $L((q))$ of $\mathrm{jq}=q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$. Let $\ell\neq p$ be a prime and let $K_\ell$ be the roof field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * ℓ))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the analogous $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)\cap\Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$, again an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, equipped with a nonzero element $j_\ell$ having the same $q$-expansion as $j$. Let $\iota_\alpha,\iota_\beta\colon K\to K_\ell$ be $L$-algebra homomorphisms such that $\iota_\alpha$ is the identity on $q$-expansions and $\iota_\beta$ acts on $q$-expansions by [`ModularCurve.qExpand L ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ (multiplication by $\ell$ on exponents). Then for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ such that the image of $A$ lies in $V$, the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ lies in the set of nonunits of $V$, and for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal is nonzero both $P(j_\ell)$ and $P(j_\ell)^{-1}$ lie in $V$, the following two conditions are equivalent: for all $f\in K$ and all $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $\bar y\neq 0$ and $f\cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$, one has $\iota_\alpha f\in V.\mathrm{nonunits}$ if and only if $\bar x=0$; and the same statement with $\iota_\beta$ in place of $\iota_\alpha$.
--
--   Each of the two conditions says that the centre of $V$, pulled back along the corresponding degeneracy embedding, is the Gauss valuation ring of $K$ over $A$ rather than the other branch ring of the mod-$p$ special fibre of $X_1(Mp)$; the theorem is thus the valuation-theoretic form of the assertion that the two legs of the Hecke correspondence at a prime $\ell\neq p$ carry a component of the special fibre to components of the same type. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_comp_eq_fst_comp_heckeDegeneracy_baseChange_of_ne_specialFibre_components_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_comp_eq_fst_comp_heckeDegeneracy_baseChange_of_ne_specialFibre_components_twoChartModel_x1_mul) to compare the degeneracy maps on the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$.
